  "metric_descriptions": {
    "curve_build": "Global-LM calibration of a square curve (23 instruments, 23 knots): ours (AAD Jacobian + templated kernel) vs QuantLib GlobalBootstrap (numerical Jacobian + object pricing)",
    "risk_full_jacobian": "Full bucketed delta ladder (our AAD + implicit-function-theorem vs QuantLib bump-and-reprice)",
    "portfolio_analytics": "Par rate + NPV + PV01 across a large swap portfolio (batched vs per-swap loop)",
    "warm_recalibration": "Stage 2: re-calibrate after a small (in-envelope) market tick -- ours (cached-Jacobian, auto envelope detection) vs QuantLib IterativeBootstrap re-bootstrap",
    "bond_sweep": "Bond universe price->YTM sweep, 5000 seasoned semiannual treasuries: ours (one batched Newton, Horner over the coupon polynomial) vs QuantLib BondFunctions::yield bond-for-bond. NB QuantLib's default path is inflated by a solver artifact (IrrFinder::derivative returns modified duration, not dP/dy, so NewtonSafe is handed a derivative ~P times too small and mostly bisects: 63 leg walks per bond, measured). The threshold is set below the ratio against the HARDER BM_BondSweep_QuantLibTuned baseline (same QuantLib pricing, correctly-scaled Newton, ~4 iterations), so this gate does not rest on that artifact.",
    "bond_book": "Curve-space bond book, 5000 bonds: ours (DF = exp(-Wx), gathered flows, sparse per-bond reduction) vs a per-bond QuantLib Bond::dirtyPrice() off a DiscountingBondEngine on the SAME discount factors (handle relinked each iteration so QuantLib cannot serve cached NPVs). No solver is involved on either side."
  },
